{"name":"Sandy Toes","hex":"#c7b8a4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sandy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered with sand.","Sprinkled with sand."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sandwich","Ellipsis of pecan sandy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sandy"},{"term":"toes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of toe"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of toe"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toe","blocks":[{"text":"Toes are the digits of the foot of a tetrapod. Animal species such as cats that walk on their toes are described as being digitigrade. Humans, and other animals that walk on the soles of their feet, are described as being plantigrade; unguligrade animals are those that walk on hooves at the tips of their toes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Toes.png/330px-Toes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toe"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Gray269.png/500px-Gray269.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Gray269.png/500px-Gray269.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bones of the right foot. Plantar surface.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray269.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u